        "title": "Quantum Computing - Field Map and Orientation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Quantum computing exploits superposition, entanglement, and interference to solve structured\nproblems in ways classical computers cannot. It does not replace classical computing — it\nextends computation into a fundamentally different physical regime, enabling algorithms\nwith no known classical equivalent for specific structured problems."
    },
